{#
    Reading progress bar (F5 reading component).
    A thin bar fixed at the top of the viewport that fills as the visitor
    scrolls through the article content. Pure progressive enhancement: hidden
    in markup, revealed by the Stimulus controller, which drives the fill via
    the --iw-reading-progress-value custom property.

    Rendered on article pages by _article_base.html.twig when enabled
    (Articles > Reading components). Reusable: include it in your own
    templates and point `selector` at any content element.

    Appearance (thickness, color) comes from --iw-reading-progress-*
    generated by the ThemeCompiler.

    Parameters (all optional):
    - selector: CSS selector of the element whose reading progress is
                measured (default '.iw-article-page')

    Decorative only (aria-hidden): announcing a constantly-updating
    progressbar would be noisy for screen readers.
#}
<div class="iw-reading-progress"
     hidden
     aria-hidden="true"
     data-controller="reading-progress"
     {%- if selector is defined and selector %} data-reading-progress-selector-value="{{ selector }}"{% endif %}>
    <div class="iw-reading-progress__bar"></div>
</div>
